ontainer\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1467799-hedge-help-please?p=1467854#post1467854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Short. Trips. The place is built to isolate, trap, and enslave you, underneath the breadth of things you can track down in there, and the more you can take advantage of that second part by better matching the Old Gods in power, the more you can beat it away from the first part.<br /> <br /> Stick together. Have a guide, preferably one who maintains high Clarity and has a kith or entitlement bonus that lets them Hedgespin to help you out.<br /> <br /> Stay on the path. Take advantage of trods, move through freehold territory whenever you can, and know the route you're taking if it's not your first trip.<br /> <br /> Be prepared to compromise and/or spend resources \u2014 taking on Goblin Debt to speed your way or giving up on your initial destination if you get Lost are both real possibilities verging on inevitabilities if given enough time.<br /> <br /> Stay positive and don't rush. The Hedge is a predator and it can smell fear. Self-explanatory.<br /> <br /> Have a ride if you can get one. Magic horses and whatnot can generally outpace the Hedge, and less of you on foot means less footpaths to get tangled up in the Briars.<br /> <br /> Be specific in your goals and have a backup plan. It's less disastrous if you fail to navigate to the Blue Alley Trod and have to circle around to the Drawbridge Clearing Hedgeway than if you get lost and have to reorient yourself before you can find Any Exit At All.</div> </div> </div> </div> Do you mind if I flat out copy and paste this, and metaphorically staple it to their foreheads? Because this is great stuff. Simple, easy to remember and helpful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1467799-hedge-help-please?p=1467854#post1467854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Frankly, I'd just encourage them to buy Wyrd dots if they intend to mess around in the Hedge a lot. Being inconvenienced by personal oaths, token drawbacks, Bedlam, Hedge-borne paradigm shifts, and Clarity damage should all provide a ready supply of Beats to bootstrap their Magic Stat upwards.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's a good point. They should be getting Beats by the truckload if I do it right. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1467799-hedge-help-please?p=1467854#post1467854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternately, take a cue from Dark Eras 2's Mysterious Frontiers writeup and have them <i>build</i> a freestanding doorway, if they're not too fussed about where they come out.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'll have to look into that, I do have Dark Era 2, but I don't remember reading that. Probably because I was more focused on Mage for that section when I read it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1467799-hedge-help-please?p=1467854#post1467854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It certainly couldn't hurt.</div> </div> </div> </div> If I do make it, I think I will post on the forums. I've made Mage Legacies (with help) before. Entitlements can't be that bad. Actually no, writing is hard. Lots of respect for Authors everywhere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1467799-hedge-help-please?p=1467854#post1467854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't have to locate an active Hedgeway, but making a new one back to Earth will require you to find (or, again, build) a closeable portal you can fit through, and generally those portals look the same in the Hedge as they do outside of it (i.e. a wooden door is a wooden door, a manhole is a manhole, a tent flap is a tent flap, etc).</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh, that makes a lot of sense. Which makes building your own door more risky because you don't know where it leads. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1467799-hedge-help-please?p=1467854#post1467854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Per the description of the Merit, a Hollow is by definition at least not in the Thorns and therefore, at worst, as plastic as the rest of the Hedge. Being inside one makes it harder to find out about you or track you down, which makes them safer for someone trying to avoid discovery in a place where finding you is as simple as succeeding at the process of finding you, but nothing about the inside of a Hollow intrinsically prevents you from getting hurt inside it.</div> </div> </div> </div> Oh, so if the Hedge decides you need a little excitement while in your Hollow, it can still harass you? I take it actually sleeping in the Hedge is a really bad idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1467799-hedge-help-please?p=1467854#post1467854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(For the record, the example of Hospitaller Bill involved a rush to get a patient from the front gate of his Hollow to a secure operating room; if he was just trying to get there to show off the place to a visitor it wouldn't have been a roll at all, but the same urgency that made that rush harder was what made the chance of failure interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div> I will keep that in mind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1467799-hedge-help-please?p=1467854#post1467854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Size Matters 2 is right there as far as scale goes, but the five-dot limit on Hollow means it may be infeasible as anything more than a general meeting space, especially given that benefiting from it requires a character to buy into it as a Motley Merit even if the &quot;extra&quot; dot does nothing.<br /> <br /> Practically speaking a large bit of Hedge infrastructure is more likely to be a series of Hollows connected through Route Zero and/or linked along one or more Stable Trods.</div> </div> </div> </div> That works better from a practical standpoint. Sure the freehold Township is hidden on the waves, but eventually everyone will be put at risk when some Hob figures it out and passes the information to the Huntsman. More Hollows means more protection.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1467799-hedge-help-please?p=1467854#post1467854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aesthetically, yes, although I'd ask on what strength that offer is enforced and to what degree \u2014 hospitality oaths are generally an individual affair, and the most prominent place in which a general &quot;make no trouble&quot; agreement is in place is the average Goblin Market, so knowing what the catch is is paramount.</div> </div> </div> </div> Hmm, I was thinking to be allowed in you must swear or the doors won't open. Breaking it might just throw you out with whatever you tried to claim Sanctuary from free to do what they want. I'd say while on the Church grounds there no physical violence, anything else goes. That's basically in theme right?<br /> On that note, how does Goblin Market &quot;make no trouble&quot; oaths work? Do most have guards on the Trods or Hedgeways that ask people to swear an oath? Or does someone agree to a oath just by entering?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-15T09:04:59-08:00","id":1467884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1467799-hedge-help-please?p=1467882#post1467882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you mind if I flat out copy and paste this, and metaphorically staple it to their foreheads? Because this is great stuff. Simple, easy to remember and helpful.</div> </div> </div> </div>By all means.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh, so if the Hedge decides you need a little excitement while in your Hollow, it can still harass you? I take it actually sleeping in the Hedge is a really bad idea. </div> </div> </div>Interacting with the Hedge prompts a roll for Hedgespinning in a Hollow the same as anywhere else, but sleeping in the Hedge isn't likely to cause you problems from the act of sleeping so much as the fact that you're unconscious in a place that can change unpredictably \u2014 your own Hollow will generally be safe, but sleeping up a tree on a commonly-used path that isn't a trod is inviting trouble. (To say nothing of the prospect of a Huntsman just walking up and taking the freebie.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hmm, I was thinking to be allowed in you must swear or the doors won't open. Breaking it might just throw you out with whatever you tried to claim Sanctuary from free to do what they want. I'd say while on the Church grounds there no physical violence, anything else goes. That's basically in theme right? </div> </div> </div>Sounds about right. Keep mechanisms in mind for this unless there's some seriously powerful mojo backing it \u2014 a case could be made that this thing is basically a powerful Hollow with some extra stuff layered on top, and Hollows are already tricky to get into as-is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On that note, how does Goblin Market &quot;make no trouble&quot; oaths work? Do most have guards on the Trods or Hedgeways that ask people to swear an oath? Or does someone agree to a oath just by entering? </div> </div> </div>For Goblin Markets it's not an oath so much as a rule enforced by bouncers. People are there to bargain, and they're to bargain with goods and services rather than naked threats \u2014 getting into an altercation that isn't part of a deal will typically have you made to stop (or at least take it outside). Even the True Fae will generally respect the sanctity of the Market, if for no other reason than it's more trouble than it's worth to find a new buyer or seller.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}